{title: In The Coming Of Messiah}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 129}

>Lyrics

Introduction

Verse 1

In the coming of Messiah,

In the coming of our King,

There is joy throughout the ages

For the blessing He will bring.

Upon the throne of David's line,

His reign shall never end.

Verse 2

Came a servant for the sinner,

Son of Man from Bethlehem.

As a kinsman and redeemer,

Conquered death and rose again.

Now with the Father glorified,

His love shall never end.

Chorus

The love of God outpoured

In mercy and in might:

Restored the soul of man,

Exchanged the wrong for right.

Removed the shackles

That had held us for so long;

Replaced despairing

With rejoicing and a song.

Verse 3

He shall come again for certain

In the manner that He rose.

He shall gather His beloved,

For His sheep, the Shepherd knows.

Unto His glory we'll arise,

And life shall never end.

Chorus

The love of God outpours

In all that He has done;

By grace transforming us:

A stranger to a son!

The Revelation of

The One who set us free

Completes the Genesis

For all eternity!

(Short solo)

Verse 4

In the coming of Messiah,

In the coming of our King,

There is joy through all creation

For the blessing He will bring.

Upon the throne of David's line,

His reign shall never end.

Our Lord shall come again!
